  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In January 2026 testimony, James G. Kushmerick said quantum computing could solve problems beyond today's classical computers and affect nearly every sector, citing modeling and simulation, optimization, and machine learning as examples. He also stated that quantum computers will significantly advance the practical use of artificial intelligence. He said NIST scientists and engineers conduct research to advance innovation in critical and emerging technologies including artificial intelligence, next-generation communications, cybersecurity, advanced manufacturing, and biotechnology, while his remarks focused on quantum information science and technology.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3"
   ],
